\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Conceptual comparison of the existing locally dependent modeling paradigm versus the decomposed gravity paradigm investigated in this study. Under the existing paradigm, models require target-city OD observations to retrain or calibrate parameters. In the decomposed paradigm, transferable origin production structures are learned from source cities, decay is recovered from target aggregate data, and attraction is mapped from local open features, enabling zero-shot transfer without target-city OD surveys.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:conceptual_framework}{{2}{3}{Conceptual comparison of the existing locally dependent modeling paradigm versus the decomposed gravity paradigm investigated in this study. Under the existing paradigm, models require target-city OD observations to retrain or calibrate parameters. In the decomposed paradigm, transferable origin production structures are learned from source cities, decay is recovered from target aggregate data, and attraction is mapped from local open features, enabling zero-shot transfer without target-city OD surveys}{figure.2}{}}
